!deck: Math Identities
!tags: Math Trigonometry Conversion
!type: Basic Math

!id: 4a0yIpmPBU
!front: Express \( \cos\theta \) in terms of \( \sin\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \cos\theta=\pm\sqrt{1-\sin^2\theta}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \cos\theta \), set by the quadrant of \( \theta \).

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, hypotenuse one, opposite leg sine theta, and adjacent leg the square root of one minus sine squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-sin.svg)
~~~

!id: 2ZWIcLdiWa
!front: Express \( \tan\theta \) in terms of \( \sin\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \tan\theta=\frac{\sin\theta}{\cos\theta}=\frac{\sin\theta}{\pm\sqrt{1-\sin^2\theta}}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \cos\theta \). Valid when \( \cos\theta\ne0 \), i.e. \( |\sin\theta|<1 \).

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, hypotenuse one, opposite leg sine theta, and adjacent leg the square root of one minus sine squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-sin.svg)
~~~

!id: 2X5lu0wbxL
!front: Express \( \cot\theta \) in terms of \( \sin\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \cot\theta=\frac{\cos\theta}{\sin\theta}=\frac{\pm\sqrt{1-\sin^2\theta}}{\sin\theta}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \cos\theta \). Valid when \( \sin\theta\ne0 \).

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, hypotenuse one, opposite leg sine theta, and adjacent leg the square root of one minus sine squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-sin.svg)
~~~

!id: AjJdEBmDDb
!front: Express \( \sec\theta \) in terms of \( \sin\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \sec\theta=\frac1{\cos\theta}=\frac1{\pm\sqrt{1-\sin^2\theta}}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \cos\theta \). Valid when \( \cos\theta\ne0 \), i.e. \( |\sin\theta|<1 \).

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, hypotenuse one, opposite leg sine theta, and adjacent leg the square root of one minus sine squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-sin.svg)
~~~

!id: 7o4jIOiYcS
!front: Express \( \csc\theta \) in terms of \( \sin\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \csc\theta=\frac1{\sin\theta}. \]
No sign choice is needed. Valid when \( \sin\theta\ne0 \).

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, hypotenuse one, opposite leg sine theta, and adjacent leg the square root of one minus sine squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-sin.svg)
~~~

