!id: WaSbzUpVHW
!front: Express \( \csc\theta \) in terms of \( \cos\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \csc\theta=\frac1{\sin\theta}=\frac1{\pm\sqrt{1-\cos^2\theta}}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \sin\theta \). Valid when \( \sin\theta\ne0 \), i.e. \( |\cos\theta|<1 \).

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, hypotenuse one, adjacent leg cosine theta, and opposite leg the square root of one minus cosine squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-cos.svg)
