!id: uZ5k7fd2AS
!front: Express \( \sin\theta \) in terms of \( \tan\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \sin\theta=\frac{\tan\theta}{\sec\theta}=\frac{\tan\theta}{\pm\sqrt{1+\tan^2\theta}}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \cos\theta \) (and hence \( \sec\theta \)) in \( \sec^2\theta=1+\tan^2\theta \). Valid wherever \( \tan\theta \) is defined.

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, adjacent leg one, opposite leg tangent theta, and hypotenuse the square root of one plus tangent squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-tan.svg)
~~~

!id: hgxXHKXWlP
!front: Express \( \cos\theta \) in terms of \( \tan\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \cos\theta=\frac1{\sec\theta}=\frac1{\pm\sqrt{1+\tan^2\theta}}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \cos\theta \) (and hence \( \sec\theta \)) in \( \sec^2\theta=1+\tan^2\theta \): positive in quadrants I and IV, negative in II and III. Valid wherever \( \tan\theta \) is defined.

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, adjacent leg one, opposite leg tangent theta, and hypotenuse the square root of one plus tangent squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-tan.svg)
~~~

!id: syXcE8cx6U
!front: Express \( \cot\theta \) in terms of \( \tan\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \cot\theta=\frac1{\tan\theta}. \]
No sign choice is needed. Valid when \( \tan\theta \) is defined and nonzero.

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, adjacent leg one, opposite leg tangent theta, and hypotenuse the square root of one plus tangent squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-tan.svg)
~~~

!id: pqgt0zOrdI
!front: Express \( \sec\theta \) in terms of \( \tan\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \sec\theta=\pm\sqrt{1+\tan^2\theta}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \cos\theta \) (and hence \( \sec\theta \)), set by the quadrant of \( \theta \). Valid wherever \( \tan\theta \) is defined.

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, adjacent leg one, opposite leg tangent theta, and hypotenuse the square root of one plus tangent squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-tan.svg)
~~~

