!front: Express \( \csc\theta \) in terms of \( \tan\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \csc\theta=\frac{\sec\theta}{\tan\theta}=\frac{\pm\sqrt{1+\tan^2\theta}}{\tan\theta}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \cos\theta \) (and hence \( \sec\theta \)) in \( \sec^2\theta=1+\tan^2\theta \). Valid when \( \tan\theta \) is defined and nonzero.

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, adjacent leg one, opposite leg tangent theta, and hypotenuse the square root of one plus tangent squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-tan.svg)
