!id: xvyiogHFLn
!front: Express \( \sin\theta \) in terms of \( \cot\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \sin\theta=\frac1{\csc\theta}=\frac1{\pm\sqrt{1+\cot^2\theta}}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \sin\theta \) (and hence \( \csc\theta \)) in \( \csc^2\theta=1+\cot^2\theta \): positive in quadrants I and II, negative in III and IV. Valid wherever \( \cot\theta \) is defined.

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, opposite leg one, adjacent leg cotangent theta, and hypotenuse the square root of one plus cotangent squared theta; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-cot.svg)
~~~

