!id: RBvpnQIXoG
!front: Express \( \sin\theta \) in terms of \( \sec\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \sin\theta=\frac{\tan\theta}{\sec\theta}=\frac{\pm\sqrt{\sec^2\theta-1}}{\sec\theta}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \tan\theta \) in \( \tan^2\theta=\sec^2\theta-1 \). Valid wherever \( \sec\theta \) is defined.

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, adjacent leg one, hypotenuse secant theta, and opposite leg the square root of secant squared theta minus one; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-sec.svg)
~~~

!id: NhJJriVRGP
!front: Express \( \cos\theta \) in terms of \( \sec\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \cos\theta=\frac1{\sec\theta}. \]
No sign choice is needed. Valid wherever \( \sec\theta \) is defined.

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, adjacent leg one, hypotenuse secant theta, and opposite leg the square root of secant squared theta minus one; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-sec.svg)
~~~

!id: BbZEbQPFeh
!front: Express \( \tan\theta \) in terms of \( \sec\theta \) only.
!back:
\[ \tan\theta=\pm\sqrt{\sec^2\theta-1}. \]
Choose \( \pm \) as the sign of \( \tan\theta \), set by the quadrant of \( \theta \). Valid wherever \( \sec\theta \) is defined.

![Right triangle with acute angle theta, adjacent leg one, hypotenuse secant theta, and opposite leg the square root of secant squared theta minus one; each function of theta is a ratio of two sides, up to sign](img/conversion-triangle-sec.svg)
~~~

